{
  "name": "cosmopolitan",
  "description": "Cosmopolitan Libc is a C/C++ library that enables 'build-once run-anywhere' functionality by outputting a POSIX-approved polyglot binary format known as Actually Portable Executable (APE). It reconfigures compilers to produce native binaries that execute without a virtual machine across Linux, Windows, macOS, and BSD systems, as well as bare-metal BIOS environments. The project provides a hermetic development environment including a custom C++ Template Library and integrated third-party tools optimized for minimal footprint and maximal performance.",
